  "qualifiedConclusions": [
    "Tinja has explicit inhabited-city wording in a primary source. Its broader urban planning area uses municipal territories, not an exact town polygon.",
    "The Ariana atlas uses Soukra as a locality in a delegation-oriented context. Its administrative and land-use maps distinguish Soukra and Bassatine sectors. This supports broad place-name usage, not equality with one sector or a surveyed point position.",
    "Tinja and Soukra name cards are consistent with broad places. Their current sector-owned base groups must be preserved by a complete finite identity proposal before changing display membership.",
    "Hrairia remains unresolved at the inhabited-quarter level. A delegation card and nearby El Agba result do not establish an alias or justify replacing nearest prayer reference398 with397."
